---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/config';

const path = '/privacy/';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | DINGDAR Casting"
  description="How DINGDAR collects, uses and protects your data when you use dingdar.com — inquiry data, analytics and your rights."
  path={path}
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    title="Privacy Policy"
    lead="This page explains what data dingdar.com collects, why we collect it, and the rights you have over your information. We keep data collection to the minimum needed to answer your inquiry and operate the site."
    img="/images/H0f45f5c3936841d5aff6bfffe8a558afY.webp"
    imgAlt="DINGDAR foundry production floor"
    ctaPrimary={{ label: 'Contact Us', href: '/contact/' }}
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:860px;">
      <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;margin-bottom:18px;">Who we are</h2>
      <p style="line-height:1.8;color:var(--ink-2);">
        {SITE.legalName} operates the website dingdar.com (and its language versions under /es/, /fr/, /ru/ and /pt/).
        This privacy policy applies to all versions of the site. If you contact us by email or WhatsApp, this policy also describes how we handle that information.
      </p>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;margin:34px 0 18px;">What we collect</h2>
      <ul style="line-height:1.9;color:var(--ink-2);">
        <li><strong>Inquiry data</strong> — the fields you submit through our contact or sample forms: name, work email, company, country, product interest, quantity and the message you write. We collect only what you choose to send.</li>
        <li><strong>Anti-spam marker</strong> — our forms include a hidden honeypot field that automated bots fill. If it is filled, the submission is discarded without being read.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical data</strong> — Google Analytics 4 collects usage statistics such as pages visited, approximate region, device type and referrer, so we can understand how the site is used.</li>
        <li><strong>Inquiry operations data</strong> — submitted inquiries may be stored in Cloudflare D1 with the source page, page language, UTM campaign fields, referrer, first landing page, a truncated user-agent and an HMAC-based IP hash. These fields help us route, protect and measure inquiry handling; they are not used as marketing-list consent.</li>
        <li><strong>Security verification</strong> — when enabled, Cloudflare Turnstile receives the verification token and relevant request information to distinguish people from automated abuse.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;margin:34px 0 18px;">How we use your data</h2>
      <ul style="line-height:1.9;color:var(--ink-2);">
        <li>To respond to your inquiry and carry out the technical review you requested.</li>
        <li>To prepare quotations, samples and orders when a project moves forward.</li>
        <li>To answer questions sent by email or WhatsApp.</li>
        <li>To measure site usage in aggregate form (Google Analytics 4).</li>
        <li>To protect the site against spam and abuse, including rate limiting based on a one-way IP hash.</li>
        <li>To attribute an inquiry to its first landing page and campaign parameters when those parameters are present.</li>
      </ul>
      <p style="line-height:1.8;color:var(--ink-2);">
        We do <strong>not</strong> sell your data, and we do not use inquiry data for marketing lists without your consent.
      </p>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;margin:34px 0 18px;">Who processes your data</h2>
      <ul style="line-height:1.9;color:var(--ink-2);">
        <li><strong>Cloudflare Pages and D1</strong> — Cloudflare hosts the site, provides the inquiry endpoint and stores inquiry records for the technical review and follow-up process.</li>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare Turnstile</strong> — when enabled, Turnstile checks form submissions for automated abuse.</li>
        <li><strong>Formspree</strong> — our inquiry endpoint forwards a copy of submitted form fields to Formspree so the existing notification workflow can deliver the inquiry to us.</li>
        <li><strong>Resend</strong> — when configured, Resend sends an internal inquiry notification and an automatic acknowledgement to the email address supplied by the buyer.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> — processes usage statistics. Google Analytics data may be processed outside your country of residence.</li>
      </ul>
      <p style="line-height:1.8;color:var(--ink-2);">
        These providers process data only for the functions described above. We do not sell your data or use inquiry data for marketing lists without your consent. If a third party becomes involved in processing your order (for example a freight forwarder), we only share the minimum details needed for that shipment.
      </p>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;margin:34px 0 18px;">Retention</h2>
      <p style="line-height:1.8;color:var(--ink-2);">
        Inquiry records are kept in Cloudflare D1 and related notification systems for the time needed to complete the review and quotation process, and for legitimate business records. Attribution and security fields are retained with the inquiry record for the same operational period unless a shorter period is required by the applicable system. If you ask us to delete your inquiry data, we will do so unless we are required by law to keep it.
      </p>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;margin:34px 0 18px;">Your rights</h2>
      <p style="line-height:1.8;color:var(--ink-2);">
        Depending on your location, you may have the right to access, correct or delete the personal data you sent us, to object to or restrict processing, and to withdraw consent at any time.
        To exercise these rights, email <a href={'mailto:' + SITE.email} style="color:var(--accent);font-weight:700;">{SITE.email}</a> with your request. We respond to verified requests within a reasonable time.
      </p>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;margin:34px 0 18px;">Cookies</h2>
      <p style="line-height:1.8;color:var(--ink-2);">
        We use cookies set by Google Analytics 4 to measure site usage. You can block or delete these cookies in your browser settings, or use Google's cookie controls. Blocking analytics cookies does not affect your ability to use the site or send an inquiry.
      </p>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;margin:34px 0 18px;">Security</h2>
      <p style="line-height:1.8;color:var(--ink-2);">
        The site is served over HTTPS. Inquiry access is restricted by an administrative password and signed session cookie. We do not store payment or account credentials. No security method is perfect, so please avoid sending passwords, payment-card data or other unnecessary sensitive information through an inquiry form.
      </p>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;margin:34px 0 18px;">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p style="line-height:1.8;color:var(--ink-2);">
        If this policy changes, the updated version will be published on this page with a revised date. Continued use of the site after changes means you accept the updated policy.
      </p>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;margin:34px 0 18px;">Contact</h2>
      <p style="line-height:1.8;color:var(--ink-2);">
        Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href={'mailto:' + SITE.email} style="color:var(--accent);font-weight:700;">{SITE.email}</a> or via our <a href="/contact/" style="color:var(--accent);font-weight:700;">contact page</a>. Last updated: 29 October 2026.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
